From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Don't unset maximized on a window that stays
 fullscreen.

Hyprland (and possibly other compositors) sends fullscreen configures with
both the fullscreen and maximized states set. A fullscreen Win32 window only
has the fullscreen state, so once such a configure is current, the next
toplevel state update sees maximized in the current state but not in the
window state and sends xdg_toplevel.unset_maximized(). Hyprland answers it
by leaving fullscreen with a maximized+tiled configure, which reaches the
application as a WM_SIZE. Wine then requests fullscreen again, and the cycle
repeats.

Since patch 0021 of this series acks fullscreen configures straight from
the requested state, the fullscreen+maximized configure becomes current
without staying in processing, so the cycle now happens on every launch.
Unreal Tournament 2004 renders into the tile-sized viewport from the
spurious WM_SIZE, and Unreal Tournament 4 drops out of fullscreen at its
splash-to-menu transition.

Fullscreen combined with maximized is the same as fullscreen (see
wayland_surface_config_is_compatible()), so leave maximized alone while
both the window and the current configure are fullscreen. Leaving
fullscreen still unsets both states.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/871
---
diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -547,8 +547,15 @@
     {
          /* First do all state unsettings, before setting new state. Some
           * Wayland compositors misbehave if the order is reversed. */
+        /* Some compositors (e.g. Hyprland) report fullscreen together with
+         * maximized. Fullscreen combined with maximized is the same as
+         * fullscreen, so keep the maximized bit while the window stays
+         * fullscreen: unsetting it makes those compositors leave fullscreen
+         * and send a tiled configure, which the application sees as a resize. */
         if (!(surface->window.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED) &&
-            (surface->current.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED))
+            (surface->current.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED) &&
+            !(surface->window.state & surface->current.state &
+              WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN))
         {
             xdg_toplevel_unset_maximized(surface->xdg_toplevel);
         }
